# Reader speed (docs/superhuman/reader.md; not run by CI, like every perf-* script): j, k and
# archive on the selected message, each timed from the key to the frame that shows the next
# conversation, on a 2,000-message fictional store at the owner's 1440x900, three panes. Each
# round prints when the reader was asked, read, prepared and ready, and whether the conversation
# came laid out ahead. Build sealwax-fixtures next to the binary, then, with a release build:
#   cargo build --release -p pronto -p sealwax-fixtures
#   tools/headless.sh 25 target/release/pronto --self-test tests/selftest/perf-reader.sealwax-test

desktop tiling
fixtures --count 2000 --seed 7 --folders spread
resize 1440 900
list-wait
list-select 0
wait-until assert-reader-selected
focus list
measure-leave j 60
measure-leave k 30
measure-leave e 20
perf-memory "end"
perf-report
